,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702583171,"data":"Below is a math problem and two attempted solutions written by a student. The correct final answer is: 6z^5+15z^4-22z^3-8z^2+17z-6\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702621325,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702628136,"data":"[Problem]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702633214,"data":"Expand $(2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1)$.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702638766,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702643653,"data":"[Answer 1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702648541,"data":"\\begin{aligned} (2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1) \u0026= 2z^2(3z^3 - 2z + 1) + 5z(3z^3 - 2z + 1) - 6(3z^3 - 2z + 1) \\\\ \u0026= 6z^5 - 4z^3 + 2z^2 + 15z^4 - 10z^2 + 5z - 18z^3 + 12z - 6 \\\\ \u0026= 6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 10z^2 + 12z - 6 \\end{aligned} \\boxed{6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 10z^2 + 12z - 6}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702658845,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.70266225,"data":"[Answer 2]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702665719,"data":"First, we need to expand the product \\((2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1)\\). We will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials or the distributive property for polynomials). \\[ (2z^2 + 5z - 6)(3z^3 - 2z + 1) \\] We distribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial: \\[ 2z^2 \\cdot 3z^3 + 2z^2 \\cdot (-2z) + 2z^2 \\cdot 1 + 5z \\cdot 3z^3 + 5z \\cdot (-2z) + 5z \\cdot 1 - 6 \\cdot 3z^3 - 6 \\cdot (-2z) - 6 \\cdot 1 \\] Now, we compute each term: \\[ 2z^2 \\cdot 3z^3 = 6z^5 \\] \\[ 2z^2 \\cdot (-2z) = -4z^3 \\] \\[ 2z^2 \\cdot 1 = 2z^2 \\] \\[ 5z \\cdot 3z^3 = 15z^4 \\] \\[ 5z \\cdot (-2z) = -10z^2 \\] \\[ 5z \\cdot 1 = 5z \\] \\[ -6 \\cdot 3z^3 = -18z^3 \\] \\[ -6 \\cdot (-2z) = 12z \\] \\[ -6 \\cdot 1 = -6 \\] Now, we combine all these terms: \\[ 6z^5 - 4z^3 + 2z^2 + 15z^4 - 10z^2 + 5z - 18z^3 + 12z - 6 \\] Combine like terms: \\[ 6z^5 + 15z^4 + (-4z^3 - 18z^3) + (2z^2 - 10z^2) + 5z + 12z - 6 \\] \\[ 6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6 \\] So, the expanded form is: \\[ \\boxed{6z^5 + 15z^4 - 22z^3 - 8z^2 + 17z - 6} \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702706364,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702711051,"data":"Write a short review (3 to 6 sentences) in the voice of the student re-checking their own two attempts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702715079,"data":"- Say which final answer each attempt reached.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702718883,"data":"- If they disagree, point to the exact step where the wrong attempt makes its mistake and explain the error briefly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702723134,"data":"- If they agree, briefly confirm the key step that makes the answer right.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702726731,"data":"- Do not mention that you were told the correct answer.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":395.702737234,"data":"- End with exactly: Therefore the final answer is \\boxed{...}.\n"}
